<node id="WAX C">
  <data key="d0">WAX C</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">WAX C is a binder used in a 2:1 weight ratio with sample material before compression into a thin sheet for XRF analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c9f812eeaa3c93f5c4d945e0ae7c91d0</data>
  <data key="d4">doi_10.1002_adv.21940.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1754208150</data>
</node>
<node id="Moving die rheometer (MDR)">
  <data key="d0">Moving die rheometer (MDR)</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Moving die rheometer (MDR) is an instrument used to determine cure characteristics of composites, manufactured by Monsanto Co., Ltd.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c9f812eeaa3c93f5c4d945e0ae7c91d0</data>
  <data key="d4">doi_10.1002_adv.21940.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1754208152</data>
</node>
<node id="Monsanto Co., Ltd.">
  <data key="d0">Monsanto Co., Ltd.</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Monsanto Co., Ltd. is a company based in OH, USA, that manufactured the moving die rheometer used in cure characterization of composites.&lt;SEP&gt;Monsanto Co., Ltd. is a company that manufactured the moving die rheometer (MDR) used for measuring the curing properties of NR and FA/NR composites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ee381638b4e2088dd8f91df9d74e6da7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9f812eeaa3c93f5c4d945e0ae7c91d0</data>
  <data key="d4">doi_10.1002_adv.21940.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1754208152</data>
</node>
<node id="OH">
  <data key="d0">OH</data>
  <data key="d1">geo</data>
  <data key="d2">OH is a location in the United States where Monsanto Co., Ltd. is based.&lt;SEP&gt;OH refers to Ohio, a state in the United States where Monsanto Co., Ltd. is located.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ee381638b4e2088dd8f91df9d74e6da7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9f812eeaa3c93f5c4d945e0ae7c91d0</data>
  <data key="d4">doi_10.1002_adv.21940.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1754208154</data>
</node>
<node id="Hobart mixer">
  <data key="d0">Hobart mixer</data>
  <data key="d1">equipment</data>
  <data key="d2">Hobart mixer is a device used to mix fly ash with NaOH solution at approximately 285 rpm for about 2 minutes during geopolymer preparation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c9f812eeaa3c93f5c4d945e0ae7c91d0</data>
  <data key="d4">doi_10.1002_adv.21940.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1754208154</data>
</node>
<node id="Ball mill">
  <data key="d0">Ball mill</data>
  <data key="d1">equipment</data>
  <data key="d2">Ball mill is used to grind the geopolymer product for about 48 hours before sieving and compounding with natural rubber.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c9f812eeaa3c93f5c4d945e0ae7c91d0</data>
  <data key="d4">doi_10.1002_adv.21940.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1754208156</data>
</node>
<node id="Hot air oven">
  <data key="d0">Hot air oven</data>
  <data key="d1">equipment</data>
  <data key="d2">Hot air oven is used to dry powders at 100°C over 14 hours and to anneal geopolymer at 65°C for 4 hours.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c9f812eeaa3c93f5c4d945e0ae7c91d0</data>
  <data key="d4">doi_10.1002_adv.21940.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1754208160</data>
</node>
<node id="Microwave">
  <data key="d0">Microwave</data>
  <data key="d1">equipment</data>
  <data key="d2">Microwave is used to further anneal the geopolymer at 450 W for 5 minutes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c9f812eeaa3c93f5c4d945e0ae7c91d0</data>
  <data key="d4">doi_10.1002_adv.21940.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1754208163</data>
</node>
<node id="200-mesh screen">
  <data key="d0">200-mesh screen</data>
  <data key="d1">equipment</data>
  <data key="d2">200-mesh screen is used to sieve geopolymer powder after grinding in the ball mill.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c9f812eeaa3c93f5c4d945e0ae7c91d0</data>
  <data key="d4">doi_10.1002_adv.21940.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1754208164</data>
</node>
<node id="ISO 10523:1994">
  <data key="d0">ISO 10523:1994</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">ISO 10523:1994 is a standard procedure used to determine the pH of the geopolymer.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c9f812eeaa3c93f5c4d945e0ae7c91d0</data>
