<edge source="Fly Ash" target="Geopolymer">
  <data key="d6">38.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Fly ash is a primary raw material used in the formation of geopolymer composites, serving as the essential aluminosilicate source required for the geopolymerization process. Through alkaline activation, fly ash reacts with an alkaline solution to initiate geopolymerization, leading to the development of a geopolymer matrix. This transformation is supported by evidence from changes in FTIR spectra and chemical composition, confirming the role of fly ash in the geopolymerization reactions. Overall, fly ash plays a critical role in providing the reactive aluminosilicate base necessary for the synthesis and structural integrity of geopolymers.</data>
  <data key="d8">chemical base,chemical reaction,chemical synthesis,chemical transformation,material composition,material transformation,raw material</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-0ff7939cdf3c7690a9b0936aae778017&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab8d7ecaf50775e77f92ac39831ef997&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e2d2a2aac672793717ce07dc518653a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b41c1604bb36ddf18d8b7e29a9c6dbe</data>
  <data key="d10">doi_10.1002_9780470456200.md&lt;SEP&gt;doi_10.1002_adv.21940.md</data>
  <data key="d11">1754208642</data>
</edge>
