<edge source="Fly Ash" target="Natural Rubber">
  <data key="d6">21.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Fly ash is compounded with natural rubber for comparative analysis with geopolymer-filled composites, indicating its role as an alternative filler.&lt;SEP&gt;Fly ash is used as a filler in natural rubber composites but shows weaker interactions and poorer thermal stability compared to geopolymer.&lt;SEP&gt;Fly ash is used as a filler in natural rubber, but results in lower curing performance compared to geopolymer due to poorer distribution and larger particle size.</data>
  <data key="d8">comparative study,composite performance,filler application,filler comparison,filler-matrix interaction,thermal degradation</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-be33bdf2df99a882230f2e5cf5a15dcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93bfd54d23eafa9bcd4bd9cf8880c1cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad60afc1fc1390582346359c09ae89a7</data>
