<edge source="NR" target="Gum NR">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Gum NR is a form of unfilled NR, serving as the baseline material for comparison with filled composites.</data>
  <data key="d8">material baseline,reference point</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-b59a215607da3067fe396c2706185342</data>
  <data key="d10">doi_10.1002_adv.21940.md</data>
  <data key="d11">1754208735</data>
</edge>
<edge source="NR" target="NR-FA10">
  <data key="d6">9.0</data>
  <data key="d7">NR-FA10 is a composite made by adding 10 phr fly ash to NR, altering its morphological and mechanical properties.</data>
  <data key="d8">composite formation,filler addition</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-b59a215607da3067fe396c2706185342</data>
  <data key="d10">doi_10.1002_adv.21940.md</data>
  <data key="d11">1754208741</data>
</edge>
<edge source="NR" target="NR-GP10">
  <data key="d6">9.0</data>
  <data key="d7">NR-GP10 is a composite formed by incorporating 10 phr geopolymer into NR, improving filler-rubber interactions.</data>
  <data key="d8">composite formation,performance enhancement</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-b59a215607da3067fe396c2706185342</data>
  <data key="d10">doi_10.1002_adv.21940.md</data>
  <data key="d11">1754208743</data>
</edge>
<edge source="NR" target="NR-GP20">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">NR-GP20 is a composite with 20 phr geopolymer in NR, within the optimal loading range for mechanical performance.</data>
  <data key="d8">composite design,optimal formulation</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-b59a215607da3067fe396c2706185342</data>
  <data key="d10">doi_10.1002_adv.21940.md</data>
  <data key="d11">1754208744</data>
</edge>
<edge source="NR" target="NR-GP30">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">NR-GP30 contains 30 phr geopolymer in NR, leading to excessive agglomeration and reduced performance.</data>
  <data key="d8">overloading,performance degradation</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-b59a215607da3067fe396c2706185342</data>
  <data key="d10">doi_10.1002_adv.21940.md</data>
  <data key="d11">1754208747</data>
</edge>
<edge source="NR" target="NR-GP40">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">NR-GP40 includes 40 phr geopolymer in NR, resulting in poor dispersion and adhesion, as seen in microscopy images.</data>
  <data key="d8">excessive filler,structural defects</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-b59a215607da3067fe396c2706185342</data>
  <data key="d10">doi_10.1002_adv.21940.md</data>
  <data key="d11">1754208757</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Tensile Strength" target="GP-Filled NR Composites">
  <data key="d6">9.0</data>
  <data key="d7">NR composites with 10 phr GP showed higher tensile strength than NR/FA composites, due to stronger GP-NR interactions.</data>
  <data key="d8">material strength,mechanical performance</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-93bfd54d23eafa9bcd4bd9cf8880c1cc</data>
  <data key="d10">doi_10.1002_adv.21940.md</data>
  <data key="d11">1754208842</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Storage Modulus (G')" target="Strain Sweep">
  <data key="d6">9.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The strain sweep test was conducted to investigate the storage modulus (G') under varying deformation levels.</data>
  <data key="d8">dynamic testing,viscoelasticity</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-ee381638b4e2088dd8f91df9d74e6da7</data>
  <data key="d10">doi_10.1002_adv.21940.md</data>
  <data key="d11">1754208622</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Thermogravimetric Analysis (TGA)" target="Thermal Stability">
  <data key="d6">10.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Thermogravimetric analysis (TGA) was used to characterize the thermal stability of GP/NR and FA/NR samples.</data>
  <data key="d8">material stability,thermal analysis</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-ee381638b4e2088dd8f91df9d74e6da7</data>
  <data key="d10">doi_10.1002_adv.21940.md</data>
  <data key="d11">1754208621</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Aluminosilicate" target="Hydrolysis">
  <data key="d6">9.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Hydrolysis breaks the -Si-O-Si- or -Si-O-Al- bonds in aluminosilicate, releasing active Al³⁺ and Si⁴⁺ species.</data>
  <data key="d8">bond breaking,chemical transformation</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-5e2d2a2aac672793717ce07dc518653a</data>
  <data key="d10">doi_10.1002_adv.21940.md</data>
  <data key="d11">1754208723</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Fourier-transform Infrared Spectroscopy" target="Si-O-T bonds">
  <data key="d6">9.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The asymmetric stretching vibrations of Si-O-T bonds at 1086 and 1100 cm⁻¹ are detected using FTIR spectroscopy.</data>
  <data key="d8">chemical bond analysis,spectral signature</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-5e2d2a2aac672793717ce07dc518653a</data>
  <data key="d10">doi_10.1002_adv.21940.md</data>
  <data key="d11">1754208721</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Fourier-transform Infrared Spectroscopy" target="Vibration of Al₂O₃">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The vibration of Al₂O₃ at 681 cm⁻¹ is identified through FTIR analysis.</data>
  <data key="d8">oxide identification,spectral detection</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-5e2d2a2aac672793717ce07dc518653a</data>
  <data key="d10">doi_10.1002_adv.21940.md</data>
  <data key="d11">1754208728</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Fourier-transform Infrared Spectroscopy" target="Al-O-Al stretching">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Al-O-Al stretching at 1007 cm⁻¹ is observed via FTIR spectroscopy, indicating bond presence in the structure.</data>
  <data key="d8">bond characterization,spectroscopic evidence</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-5e2d2a2aac672793717ce07dc518653a</data>
  <data key="d10">doi_10.1002_adv.21940.md</data>
  <data key="d11">1754208731</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Nucleation" target="Hydrolysis">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The release of active Al³⁺ and Si⁴⁺ species through hydrolysis enables the formation of nuclei, leading to nucleation.</data>
  <data key="d8">phase initiation,reaction precursor</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-5e2d2a2aac672793717ce07dc518653a</data>
  <data key="d10">doi_10.1002_adv.21940.md</data>
  <data key="d11">1754208711</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Nucleation" target="Oligomerization">
  <data key="d6">9.0</data>
  <data key="d7">After nucleation, aluminosilicate oligomers form, indicating that nucleation precedes oligomerization in the geopolymerization sequence.</data>
  <data key="d8">phase transition,process progression</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-5e2d2a2aac672793717ce07dc518653a</data>
  <data key="d10">doi_10.1002_adv.21940.md</data>
  <data key="d11">1754208713</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Oligomerization" target="Polymerization">
  <data key="d6">9.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Oligomerization produces aluminosilicate oligomers that are linked during polymerization to form polysialate chains.</data>
  <data key="d8">chemical progression,network formation</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-5e2d2a2aac672793717ce07dc518653a</data>
  <data key="d10">doi_10.1002_adv.21940.md</data>
  <data key="d11">1754208714</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Polymerization" target="Polysialate">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Polysialate chains (-Al-O-Si-) are formed during the polymerization stage of geopolymerization.</data>
  <data key="d8">chemical bonding,structural product</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-5e2d2a2aac672793717ce07dc518653a</data>
  <data key="d10">doi_10.1002_adv.21940.md</data>
  <data key="d11">1754208718</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Polymerization" target="Polysialate siloxo">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Polysialate siloxo (-Al-O-Si-Si-) chains are formed during polymerization, indicating specific structural configurations.</data>
  <data key="d8">chain formation,molecular structure</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-5e2d2a2aac672793717ce07dc518653a</data>
  <data key="d10">doi_10.1002_adv.21940.md</data>
  <data key="d11">1754208721</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Polymerization" target="Polysialate disiloxo">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Polysialate disiloxo (-Al-O-Si-Si-Si-) chains are formed during polymerization, representing extended siloxo structures.</data>
  <data key="d8">molecular structure,network extension</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-5e2d2a2aac672793717ce07dc518653a</data>
  <data key="d10">doi_10.1002_adv.21940.md</data>
  <data key="d11">1754208725</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Cure Curve" target="Cross-Linking">
